Looking at this problem, I need to simulate the described coloring process on an N×N grid.

**Approach:** Simulate each operation sequentially — for each i from 1 to N, compute j = N+1-i, and if i ≤ j, fill the square from (i,i) to (j,j) with '#' (odd i) or '.' (even i), overwriting previous colors.

**Complexity:** N ≤ 50, and each iteration does at most O(N²) work, so total O(N³) = O(125,000) — perfectly efficient.

